# L §5.7's grammar: `"place" [CUR | ID | "any" | "one"] [sign] ...   (unit and sign: required, LOAD-PLACEKIND, not
# LOAD-PARSE)` (pick P44, the twin of L5_7_place_kind_no_unit_sign): `kind bar: place` with neither is LOAD-PLACEKIND at
# its line. refcore 2.1.7 refused it as LOAD-PARSE, expecting a unit.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind bar: place
input y: int
ask q: y

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  y = 1
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PLACEKIND place kind bar has no unit or sign rule (m.tally:9)
